Z||000000||Bill H||10-19-2000||10:38 PM|||| I need a motor for my formula I would like a 3.1. If any one has purchased one please let me know your story good and bad.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||10:45 PM||||I took the 2.8 out with a bad rod knock. I put in the rebuilt engine as a 3.2. total investment was right arround $2000 or so. true I could get a 3.4 crate for $1650, but then you start adding in things, and it'll shoot up higher. if I had it to do over again, and was planing on doing it (instead of, only means of transportation goes knock knock knock). I would have saved up an extra grand and gone for the 3.4 install. just to make sure I had enough to cover what ever happened. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maninblack||10-19-2000||11:19 PM||||what would a 3.1 brings the horsepower up to?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||10-20-2000||09:41 AM||||it all matters on the cam. If you go for high flow exhaust, and either headers or open up the manifolds, with a strong cam, I can see you pulling 200 hp at the flywheel. I built mine to be more on the torque side. so I should be arround 175 hp, with arround 205 ft lbs of torque at the flex plate, stock exhaust an all. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-20-2000||10:02 AM||||The major benefit of stroking a 2.8 to a 3.1 is in the additional torque.  Don't get hung up on HP numbers.<P>My daughter had an 86 RX7 which was rated at around the same hp as my 2.8 but the torque sucked.||||reg||1
